# Monorepo & Packages

## Purpose

Keep the pnpm + Turborepo workspace consistent: every publishable package looks the same,
depends on the right tier, exports a stable surface, and stays tree-shakable.

## Why it exists

These are published open-source packages. The `package.json` `exports` map and the barrel
files are the public contract. Inconsistent manifests, hardcoded internal versions, or leaked
internals break consumers and the release tooling.

## Monorepo layout

- `packages/core` -> `@lensjs/core`: engine + React dashboard (`src/ui`).
- `packages/express|fastify|nestjs|adonis` -> `@lensjs/<framework>`: adapters.
- `packages/handlers` -> `@lensjs/watchers`: ORM/mailer integrations.
- `packages/docs` -> `docs`: VitePress site (private, not published).
- `shared/date` -> `@lensjs/date`; `shared/typescript-config` -> `@lensjs/typescript-config`.
- `apps/*`: runnable example apps per framework (private, not published).

Note: folder name may differ from package name (`packages/handlers` publishes `@lensjs/watchers`).

## Commands (from repo root)

- Install: `pnpm install` — NEVER `npm install` / `yarn`.
- Build (respects the dep graph): `pnpm build`. Dev: `pnpm dev`. UI dev: `pnpm run dev:front`.
- Test: `pnpm test`. Turbo runs `test` after `^build` + `check-types`
  ([turbo.json](mdc:turbo.json)).

## Cross-package dependencies

- Reference internal packages with `"workspace:*"` (e.g. `"@lensjs/core": "workspace:*"`).
- Never hardcode a published version for an internal package.
- Never import another package by relative path across package boundaries. Import the public
  `@lensjs/*` entry. The `../../core/dist/...` import in
  [define_config.ts](mdc:packages/adonis/src/define_config.ts) is known debt — do not copy it.

## Dependency tiering (critical for bundle size)

Model the tiers on [handlers package.json](mdc:packages/handlers/package.json):

- `dependencies`: only lightweight runtime needs + workspace primitives (`@lensjs/core`,
  `@lensjs/date`). Core adds `denque`, `libsql`, `luxon`, `sql-formatter`, `stack-utils`.
- `devDependencies`: ORMs/tools used only for TYPES at build time (`prisma`, `kysely`) and
  `@lensjs/typescript-config`, `vitest`.
- `peerDependencies` (+ `peerDependenciesMeta.optional`): the user-supplied driver/framework
  (e.g. `nodemailer` optional peer in handlers; `fastify`/`@fastify/static` peers in the
  fastify adapter). The consumer picks the version.

Adapters may keep their framework as a normal `dependency` (express) OR a peer (fastify) —
match the sibling package you are extending. `@lensjs/express` is the template manifest.

## Publishable package.json conventions (match `@lensjs/express`)

- Scope under `@lensjs/*`; `"type": "module"`.
- Dual output via `exports`:

```json
"exports": { ".": { "require": "./dist/index.cjs", "import": "./dist/index.js" } }
```

- Set `"main"`, `"types"`, `"files": ["dist"]`, `"publishConfig": { "access": "public" }`.
- Include `repository.directory`, `homepage`, `bugs`, and relevant `keywords` for
  discoverability. (Fastify's manifest is currently missing these — fix, don't imitate.)
- Build with `tsup` (ESM + CJS + `.d.ts`, `target: node18`, `skipNodeModulesBundle`,
  `splitting: false`) — see [tsup.config.ts](mdc:tsup.config.ts). Adonis is the intentional
  exception (builds with `tsc` + stubs per AdonisJS package conventions).
- Do NOT commit `dist/` (gitignored, produced by build).

## Barrels, public surface & tree-shaking

- Each package exposes ONE `.` entry; do not add ad-hoc subpath exports.
- Re-export the public surface from an `index.ts` barrel. Keep it minimal.
- Use SELECTIVE re-exports to hide internals while still allowing tests to import them
  directly: e.g. [handlers query barrel](mdc:packages/handlers/src/query/index.ts) exports
  `export * from "./prisma"` (helpers are module-private) but only
  `export { createSequelizeHandler }` from `sequelize.ts` (whose helpers are public for tests).
- Tree-shaking relies on ESM output + the `import` condition + named exports; never introduce
  import side effects at module top level.

## Backward compatibility & public API stability

- Adding an optional field / new named export = `minor`.
- Changing a signature, removing/renaming an export, or changing an `exports` path = `major`
  (requires a `major` changeset — see `release.mdc`).
- When in doubt, add a new symbol rather than changing an existing one.

## AI must never

- Run `npm`/`yarn` in this repo, or hand-edit `version`/`CHANGELOG.md`.
- Add a heavy dependency to a `dependencies` block when it can be a dev/peer dependency.
- Add a new subpath to `exports` or change an existing export path without a `major` changeset.
- Leak an internal symbol into a package barrel just to reach it from another package — use the
  public API or move the code.
